- `line 101` - check CANNOT FAIL / STATUS CODE REPORTING WRAPPER. Exact input at line-54 boundary: `find_trial_objects(A) -> [('NCT00000001_a','{name:"Alpha"}')]`, `find_trial_objects(B) -> [('NCT00000001_b','{name:"Beta"}')]`, both files matching `*_REVIEW*.html`, neither preceded by `NULLED:`. Consequence: the script reports a LIVE-vs-LIVE serious conflict but exits `0`, so a gate cannot fail.

- `line 36` - instrument reads a DIFFERENT COPY. Exact input: `is_nulled('"NULLED:NCT00000001":{name:"Alpha"}\n"NCT00000001_x":{name:"Alpha"}', 'NCT00000001', '{name:"Alpha"}')` for the second/live occurrence. Consequence: `html.find(obj)` selects the first identical NULLED object and marks the live record inert, hiding live conflicts.

- `line 29` - selector reads the wrong `name` binding. Exact input: `trial_name('{display_name:"Wrong",name:"Right"}')`. Consequence: returns `"Wrong"` because `name:"` is matched inside `display_name`, so conflicts can be created or missed against non-trial-name data.

- `line 51` - selector is keyed to overbroad text. Exact input path: `F:\rapidmeta-ssot-shell\not_backup_REVIEW.html`. Consequence: a real review file is skipped solely because `"backup"` appears anywhere in its path.

